<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Blyvoor Q1 pre-capex net profit halved.</title>
<headline>Blyvoor Q1 pre-capex net profit halved.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  9.97 vs 18.81</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 12.36 vs 6.26</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			    1,457 vs 1,529</p>
<p>    - surface				    454 vs 411</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - underground			  246,000 vs 286,000</p>
<p>    - surface				821,000 vs 706,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - underground			     5.92 vs 5.35</p>
<p>    - surface				   0.55 vs 0.58</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			   54,348 vs 54,061</p>
<p>    - surface				 34,804 vs 25,190</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)			   53,502 vs 55,860</p>
<p>Full name: Blyvooruitzicht Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Caving of the shaft ore pass system at Doornfontein resulted in redued tonnages from underground. The new ore pass sytem will be operational by July 1997. Stoppage of some low grade panels on Doornfontein resulted in higher underground grade.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
